n}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow notice that the given curve is $\\text{unbounded},$ representing $\\text{a spiral}$ that is traversed $\\text{counterclockwise}.$ Thus, we must have $a\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, notice that the spiral is traversed toward $\\text{infinity}.$\n\nHence, to insure that ${e}^{at}\\to \\infty ,$ we require $a>0.$" 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186167249 1068 #edb/ref 17592186164537 13194139533415 17592186045585 false] [17592186167249 1068 #edb/ref 17592186164544 13194139533415 17592186045585 false] [17592186167249 1068 #edb/ref 17592186307794 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186167249 1068 #edb/ref 17592186308238 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186167249 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186167249 1071 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-2x(t)-5y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=5x(t)-2y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda =-2\\pm 5\\text{i}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.$\\,$\nSince \n{{field-1}},\nthe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-2}}." 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186167249 1071 "${x^{′}(t) =-2x(t) - 5y(t); y^{′}(t) = 5x(t) - 2y(t)$\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $λ =-2 ± 5\\textrm{i}$. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\nSince\n{{field-1}},\nthe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-2}}." 13194139533415 17592186045585 false] [17592186167249 1074 "Let $v=p+q\\text{i},$ where $p,q\\in {R}^{2},$ be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =a+b\\text{i}.$\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t)=v{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operat