})_{n}-\\frac{0.5(({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n})^{3}-({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-0.272}{1.5(({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n})^{2}-1}.\n$$\n\nApplying several iterations of Newton's method starting with $y(1)=-1.4,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({y}_{\\text{new}})_{1} & =-1.4 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{2} & ≈-1.274\\,227 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{3} & ≈-1.251\\,778 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{4} & ≈-1.251\\,069\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(2)≈-1.25,$ rounded to two decimal places." 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186229667 1068 #edb/ref 17592186228166 13194139533415 17592186045585 false] [17592186229667 1068 #edb/ref 17592186307692 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186229667 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186229667 1071 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-2x(t)+1,\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n| $[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)$ |  |  |" 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186229667 1071 "${x^{′}(t) = 2y(t); y^{′}(t) =-2x(t) + 1,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: $e^{At} = \\begin{bmatrix}\\cos (2t) & \\sin (2t) \\\\ -\\sin (2t) & \\cos (2t)\\end{bmatrix}$, where $A = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$.*\n\n| $\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix} = \\frac{1}{2}$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n|  | $3\\sin (2t)$ |  |  |" 13194139533415 1