d}\\,5\\beta =-5,\n$$\n\nso, we have\n\n$$\n\\alpha =8\\,\\text{and}\\,\\beta =-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=8x{e}^{-4x}-{e}^{x}.\n$$" 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186308402 1068 #edb/ref 17592186307591 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186308402 1068 #edb/ref 17592186307593 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186308402 1068 #edb/ref 17592186307642 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186308402 1068 #edb/ref 17592186307799 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186308402 1068 #edb/ref 17592186307910 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186308402 1068 #edb/ref 17592186307925 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186308402 1068 #edb/ref 17592186308068 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186308402 1068 #edb/ref 17592186308126 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186308402 1068 #edb/ref 17592186308151 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186308402 1068 #edb/ref 17592186308288 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186308402 1069 "q-333159" 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186308402 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186308402 1071 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-3x(t)-2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-3,$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[1,-1]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[1,0]^{T},$ respectively. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]={c}_{1}\\cdot {{field-1}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}\\cdot {{field-2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny={{field-3