lutions ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?" 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186308605 1072 #uuid "0a96ede4-5f22-51e8-acbb-7d3f2a89ee5f" 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186308605 1074 "Given a linear system ${x}^{′}=Ax,$ where $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $Φ(t)$ of the system is an $n\\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our case, we have a $2\\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}2t \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}=[\\begin{aligned}2t{e}^{3t} \\\\ -{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental could be written as\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{3t} & 2t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & -{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Note:** The columns of $Φ$ can be written in any order." 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186308606 1068 #edb/ref 17592186307533 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186308606 1069 "q-334330" 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186308606 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186308606 1071 "$$\n{x}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]x,\\,{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t},\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?" 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] [17592186308606 1072 #uuid "3e83b1a2-7579-5dd1-bddd-671f2c156572" 13194139533415 17592186045585 true] 